  <Prose>
    {/* Adapted from netsci2026.com/about. Spirit paragraph is a DRAFT — wording to be agreed with the chairs. */}
    <p>
      <strong>NetSci</strong> is the flagship conference of the
      <a href="https://netscisociety.net">Network Science Society</a> and the premier venue for sharing
      and discussing discoveries, ideas, and emerging challenges in network science. Its program spans
      the many ways networks shape our world: social and information networks, epidemics and public
      health, ecological and biological systems, the brain, infrastructure, and AI-driven systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      NetSci 2027 is organised by the Center Synergy of Systems (SynoSys) at TU Dresden and takes place
      in <strong>Dresden, Germany, from 17 to 21 May 2027</strong>: satellites and the school on
      17–18 May, followed by the main conference from 18 to 21 May.
    </p>
    <p>
      This edition is forward-looking. We want NetSci 2027 to break boundaries between disciplines and
      communities, and to put young researchers at the centre of the program.
    </p>
    <h2>What to expect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keynote lectures from leaders across the field.</li>
      <li>Contributed talks and poster sessions.</li>
      <li>Community-organised satellite symposia and the NetSci school (17–18 May).</li>
    </ul>
